    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a and b supply the two separate conditions: the radicand x-2≥0 and the denominator x-5≠0. Part c asks the student to combine them, giving x≥2 with the single point 5 removed from that interval. This is a routine link of two familiar domain restrictions, and the only real decision is that both must hold together. It needs slightly more than the single-restriction questions, but it is more scaffolded than the unprompted mixed domains in p39-q12.",
